      "title": "Canonical publication-output identity can be bypassed with a dot-segment path alias",
      "facts": [
        "readPin15 accepts file containing /./ because realpath(file) is compared with resolve(file), without requiring the declared file to be that canonical path.",
        "Both assertNoPublicationPointers15 and the F required-file walk compare raw .file strings.",
        "Actual verifyAfterFrame15 rejects a direct sidecar reference in the required journal, but accepts a reference to the very same sidecar file under a dot-segment alias."
      ],
      "impact": "The frozen F/C/S no-back-reference contract is not independently enforced for actual file identity.",
      "minimumCorrection": [
        "Use one strict canonical/noalias pin identity for reads, same-pin checks and all publication/required-file pointer checks.",
        "Reject alias spellings instead of silently normalizing them; retain regular/nlink/hash/byte protections.",
        "Add actual complete-frame alias regression plus canonical positive/direct-negative controls."
      ],
      "actualProductionCounterexample": true,
      "needsFutureReg5ToProve": false
    },
    {
      "id": "H9-IR02",
      "priority": "P2",
      "status": "confirmed-open",
      "file": "tools/rust-r4ghi/tax15-readonly/facts15.mjs",
      "lines": [
        99,
        100
      ],
      "title": "Native FI rollback accepts session changes outside the original raw5 semantics",
      "facts": [
        "An actual two-database/139-table fixture with idle_expires_at reduced from 01:00 to 00:30 is accepted while all other native predicates hold.",
        "A session with last_seen_at unchanged, but row_version +1 and xmin changed, is also accepted.",
        "The actual protected exactRawTouch export rejects both; its last_seen must advance strictly and idle expiry must not decrease. A valid forward touch is accepted by both."
      ],
      "impact": "The independent native reader can attest raw-session-only rollback for mutations the existing raw5 verifier would reject.",
      "minimumCorrection": [
        "Retain the exact old raw5 semantics: active same actor/session, stable other columns, row_version +1, finite strictly advancing last_seen, updated==last_seen, nondecreasing idle expiry bounded by absolute, changed xmin.",
        "Keep zero-delta rollback valid, forbid managed coflush/audit/security/domain rows, and add both actual function negatives."
      ],
      "actualProductionCounterexample": true,
      "needsFutureReg5ToProve": false
    }
